From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gallivm: honor host CPU features on AArch64

An Arm CPU name can imply SVE even when Linux does not expose it. Pass
LLVM's kernel-aware host feature map, including disabled features, just as
on 32-bit Arm. A physical llvmpipe core stopped at an SVE index instruction
on a system without HWCAP_SVE. This does not qualify native GPU support.

--- a/src/gallium/auxiliary/gallivm/lp_bld_misc.cpp
+++ b/src/gallium/auxiliary/gallivm/lp_bld_misc.cpp
@@ -316,7 +316,7 @@
 lp_build_fill_mattrs(std::vector<std::string> &MAttrs)
 {
 
-#if DETECT_ARCH_ARM
+#if DETECT_ARCH_ARM || DETECT_ARCH_AARCH64
    /* llvm-3.3+ implements sys::getHostCPUFeatures for Arm,
     * which allows us to enable/disable code generation based
     * on the results of cpuid on these architectures.
